{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Scraping Data from a Real Website + pandas\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook requests a webpage, uses BeautifulSoup to find a table, collects its headings and rows, places them in a pandas DataFrame, and downloads a CSV.\n",
        "\n",
        "The table lookup checks the headings instead of relying on a table number or CSS class. That avoids the lookup errors caused by changes to Wikipedia's page layout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Import the libraries"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from bs4 import BeautifulSoup\n",
        "import requests\n",
        "import pandas as pd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Fetch the webpage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "url = \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_largest_companies_in_the_United_States_by_revenue\"\n",
        "\n",
        "page = requests.get(url)\n",
        "page.raise_for_status()  # Stop with an error if the webpage request failed\n",
        "soup = BeautifulSoup(page.text, \"html\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Status code:\", page.status_code)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Find the company table\n",
        "\n",
        "The table index can change. This loop finds a table whose headings include Rank, Name, and Industry."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "tables = soup.find_all(\"table\")\n",
        "print(\"Tables found:\", len(tables))\n",
        "\n",
        "table = None\n",
        "for possible_table in tables:\n",
        "    headings = [heading.get_text(\" \", strip=True) for heading in possible_table.find_all(\"th\")]\n",
        "    if \"Rank\" in headings and \"Name\" in headings and \"Industry\" in headings:\n",
        "        table = possible_table\n",
        "        break\n",
        "\n",
        "if table is None:\n",
        "    raise ValueError(\"The company table was not found. The webpage structure may have changed.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Company table found.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Get the table headings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "world_titles = table.find_all(\"th\")\n",
        "world_table_titles = [title.text.strip() for title in world_titles]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(world_table_titles)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Create an empty DataFrame with those headings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "df = pd.DataFrame(columns=world_table_titles)\n",
        "df"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Get the rows and add them to the DataFrame\n",
        "\n",
        "Each table row is read from its `td` cells and added to the next DataFrame row. The length check skips rows that do not match the headings."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "column_data = table.find_all(\"tr\")\n",
        "\n",
        "for row in column_data:\n",
        "    row_data = row.find_all(\"td\")\n",
        "    individual_row_data = [data.text.strip() for data in row_data]\n",
        "\n",
        "    if len(individual_row_data) == len(world_table_titles):\n",
        "        length = len(df)\n",
        "        df.loc[length] = individual_row_data\n",
        "\n",
        "df"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 7. Review the scraped data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"Rows and columns:\", df.shape)\n",
        "display(df.head())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 8. Save the data as a CSV and download it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "df.to_csv(\"Companies.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "from google.colab import files\n",
        "files.download(\"Companies.csv\")"
      ]
    }
  ],
